    <h2>What this page could not verify<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="warn">
      Four things, stated plainly so you know which parts of the page are reconstruction and which are reads.
      <br><br>
      <b>1. The button-bank sequence.</b> We can see the panel, the green lights and the doors opening, but neither recording preserves which button was pressed in which order, and the game gives no printed clue. No order is printed here because any order we gave you would be invented.
      <br><br>
      <b>2. The equation panel.</b> The display <b>8+4+6 = 6+7+4</b> with marks under three digits is visible and readable, but neither player interacts with it and the level completes without it. Whether it is a red herring, an optional sequence, or the input for something we never found, we do not know.
      <br><br>
      <b>3. The Glass shard and the Package.</b> Both are picked up, both are labelled in the inventory, and neither is used in any shot we captured. The obvious guess is that the shard cuts the package open, and that the package holds the key — but neither recording shows either action, so it is a guess, not a read, and it is not printed as a step.
      <br><br>
      <b>4. The chapter epilogue.</b> The results panel after room 26 is the standard one, with no chapter card in either recording. If the game plays a Chapter 2 epilogue after the panel, it happens behind a button neither recording pressed.
